  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 5.2,
      "end": 12.2,
      "text": "On 275 and 285. Also in stereo on VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.2,
      "end": 28.38,
      "text": "Hi there. Good evening to you. TV on Radio Thomas Vance here. Welcome once again to the Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.38,
      "end": 36.02,
      "text": "This evening the only session that AC DC recorded for Radio 1 way back in 1976. We also have the first session recorded by Syd Barrett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.02,
      "end": 42.02,
      "text": "Original Floyd member. That one was put together in the 70s. Actually in 1970. Also Praying Mantis.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.31,
      "end": 58.89,
      "text": "We've got classic cuts from Motorhead, Ted Nugent, Todd Rundgren, among others,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 58.95,
      "end": 61.67,
      "text": "and new releases by Frank Zappa, Wishbone Ash, and The Pretenders.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 62.49,
      "end": 64.57,
      "text": "My show from Anne Nightingale tonight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 64.81,
      "end": 67.97,
      "text": "Lucky lady got to interview that Miss Hine from The Pretenders.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.34,
      "end": 73.32,
      "text": "Also, the Friday Night Connection later, but right now you're not in bad company.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 661.23,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 661.23,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 666.23,
      "end": 668.37,
      "text": "That's the first of three by Praying Mantis tonight.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 668.37,
      "end": 674.17,
      "text": "That's the session we put together, what, round about last, well, the 31st of the 10th of 1979, to be precise.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 674.57,
      "end": 675.63,
      "text": "It was called Captured City.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 678.36,
      "end": 681.48,
      "text": "And prior to that, something that came out in 1974",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 681.48,
      "end": 683.76,
      "text": "on the album Bad Company by Bad Company,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 683.86,
      "end": 684.94,
      "text": "the track was Rock Steady.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 685.48,
      "end": 688.32,
      "text": "And that was for John Wilson of [redacted address],",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 688.46,
      "end": 689.38,
      "text": "Bramley and Leith.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 690.4,
      "end": 692.42,
      "text": "Quick reminder that if there are any tracks",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 692.42,
      "end": 694.98,
      "text": "that you remember from the dim and distant past,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 697.14,
      "end": 699.38,
      "text": "if you'd like us to get out of the BBC Record Library,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 699.48,
      "end": 701.2,
      "text": "just write to us here at the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 701.72,
      "end": 705.02,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1, London, W1A4WW,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 705.96,
      "end": 706.94,
      "text": "and we'll go digging.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 706.94,
      "end": 711.6,
      "text": "as indeed we dug for this",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 711.6,
      "end": 713.22,
      "text": "because many people wanted to hear it",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 713.22,
      "end": 715.98,
      "text": "the 1976 session from ACDC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 715.98,
      "end": 720.18,
      "text": "couple of tracks out of the archives",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 720.18,
      "end": 1313.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 720.18,
      "end": 1313.02,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1313.02,
      "end": 1314.24,
      "text": "circa 1976",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1314.24,
      "end": 1317.02,
      "text": "recorded during the first visit to this country",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1317.02,
      "end": 1319.36,
      "text": "by the Australian band called ACDC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1319.36,
      "end": 1321.26,
      "text": "Angus Young on the lead guitar",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1321.26,
      "end": 1322.6,
      "text": "Malcolm Young on the rhythm guitar",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1322.6,
      "end": 1323.52,
      "text": "Mark Evans bass",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1323.52,
      "end": 1324.64,
      "text": "Philip Rudd on the drums",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1324.64,
      "end": 1326.5,
      "text": "Bon Scott on the lead vocals",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1326.5,
      "end": 1327.9,
      "text": "the tracks you heard were Livewire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1327.9,
      "end": 1329.6,
      "text": "and Can I Sit Next To You",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1329.6,
      "end": 1331.64,
      "text": "I'll never forget the day that I first met that band",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1331.64,
      "end": 1334.72,
      "text": "and it was way before they even had any product out in this country,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1334.9,
      "end": 1336.68,
      "text": "or indeed before they'd done any touring.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1337.16,
      "end": 1340.28,
      "text": "And I met this geezer in the funny little schoolboy clothes,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1340.34,
      "end": 1343.46,
      "text": "and I really thought they were a joke until I went to see them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1343.9,
      "end": 1345.14,
      "text": "And then I changed my mind.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1345.58,
      "end": 1353.38,
      "text": "From Joe's Garage X 2 and 3, the track called Keep It Greasy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1832.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.0,
      "end": 1832.51,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1832.51,
      "end": 1835.59,
      "text": "We can only ever play extracts of Mr. Zapper's works these days",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1835.59,
      "end": 1839.88,
      "text": "because very little of it can actually go out on radio.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1839.88,
      "end": 1843.1,
      "text": "that has recorded product to be played in the home,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1843.22,
      "end": 1844.72,
      "text": "I would heartily recommend it.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1844.76,
      "end": 1845.92,
      "text": "His new album's out on CBS.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1854.92,
      "end": 1855.62,
      "text": "It's 10.30.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1855.92,
      "end": 1857.54,
      "text": "I've got a couple of letters in front of me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1857.58,
      "end": 1858.96,
      "text": "This one comes from Martin Lawson,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1859.34,
      "end": 1862.78,
      "text": "who lives at [redacted address], Chipstead in Seven Oaks in Kent.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1863.12,
      "end": 1864.28,
      "text": "He's going to be a happy man.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1864.62,
      "end": 1868.56,
      "text": "As is Keith Fleeman of [redacted address],",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1869.0,
      "end": 1871.1,
      "text": "Streeckley, Sutton Coalfield in the West Midlands.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1872.04,
      "end": 1875.4,
      "text": "And they're just two of the people",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1875.4,
      "end": 1877.74,
      "text": "who I think are going to be extraordinarily happy now",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1877.74,
      "end": 1880.26,
      "text": "when we dig out of the archives from 1970,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1880.6,
      "end": 1882.78,
      "text": "some classics by Sid Barrett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1883.2,
      "end": 1888.0,
      "text": "...of the archives from way back in 1970.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1888.0,
      "end": 2225.16,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1888.0,
      "end": 2225.16,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2225.16,
      "end": 2226.72,
      "text": "The man that put together the Pink Floyd",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2226.72,
      "end": 2229.58,
      "text": "at Camberwell Art School way back in 1965.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2230.52,
      "end": 2232.32,
      "text": "Sid Barrett, the Traxy Herbert Terrapin,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2232.42,
      "end": 2233.66,
      "text": "which incidentally was also the name",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2233.66,
      "end": 2236.5,
      "text": "of the Sid Barrett UK Appreciation Society",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2236.5,
      "end": 2237.58,
      "text": "monthly newsletter,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2237.7,
      "end": 2239.26,
      "text": "whether that's still going or not, I don't know.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2239.8,
      "end": 2241.68,
      "text": "And the track before that was called Baby Lemonade.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2241.68,
      "end": 2243.86,
      "text": "On the session, we know that Dave Gilmour",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2243.86,
      "end": 2245.88,
      "text": "was there in 1970, as was drummer",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2245.88,
      "end": 2248.0,
      "text": "Jerry Shirley. And we rather think",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2248.0,
      "end": 2249.86,
      "text": "that Rick Wright was there as well, but we're not too",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2249.86,
      "end": 2251.78,
      "text": "sure. More from Sid later.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2252.04,
      "end": 2253.92,
      "text": "But right now, here's something new from the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2253.92,
      "end": 2255.56,
      "text": "latest album by Wishbone Ash,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2255.94,
      "end": 2257.84,
      "text": "which is called Just Testing. This is",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2257.84,
      "end": 2263.24,
      "text": "haunting me. A couple of tracks from an album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2263.24,
      "end": 2922.6,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2263.24,
      "end": 2922.6,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2923.32,
      "end": 2925.22,
      "text": "that's coming out on the 18th of January.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2925.4,
      "end": 2927.44,
      "text": "Wishbone Ash, the album's called Just Testing,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2927.6,
      "end": 2928.86,
      "text": "the tracks you heard were Lifeline",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2928.86,
      "end": 2931.22,
      "text": "and Haunting Me. And on the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2931.22,
      "end": 2933.44,
      "text": "18th of January, they actually start a month",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2933.44,
      "end": 2935.26,
      "text": "long tour of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2935.26,
      "end": 2938.8,
      "text": "Scotland and England, but looking down the date sheet, they're not going to go to Wales or Ireland.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2939.32,
      "end": 2942.36,
      "text": "So it looks like you're going to have to cross some provincial borders if you want to see them.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2942.76,
      "end": 2946.06,
      "text": "So that was Wishbone Ash, and that was specially for a gentleman by the name of Mark",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2946.06,
      "end": 2951.22,
      "text": "and his two roommates, that's, I think, Gary and Joey, from Mum and the Children,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2951.48,
      "end": 2956.84,
      "text": "and also for a whole stack of people from Graham, of [redacted address], Harlow and Essex,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2957.26,
      "end": 2961.78,
      "text": "wanted me to say hello to everybody at the Harlow Technical College, including Andy John Quiff's chick.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2961.78,
      "end": 2965.0,
      "text": "Oh, maybe, yeah. I thought for a minute it was chic, but actually it's chick.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2965.5,
      "end": 2966.26,
      "text": "It may be chic.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2966.52,
      "end": 2968.82,
      "text": "Jane, Mandy, Al, Jerry, Benny, Sue and Nigel,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2969.22,
      "end": 2971.46,
      "text": "and a Steve, and also da brother, Martin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2978.59,
      "end": 2980.73,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show, here's Praying Mantis.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2980.73,
      "end": 3415.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2980.73,
      "end": 3415.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3542.2,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3420.0,
      "end": 3542.2,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3542.2,
      "end": 3545.08,
      "text": "That's Motorhead, the title track from the album of the same name.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3545.22,
      "end": 3548.76,
      "text": "Especially for all the lads at LWC, Lord Wandsworth College.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3549.08,
      "end": 3550.22,
      "text": "Dating Stoke and Hance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3550.92,
      "end": 3554.28,
      "text": "Particularly Bob and Morass, I think it's Noobs, Jeff, Cy,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3554.5,
      "end": 3556.76,
      "text": "Mick who didn't take it, and Dave who wrote the letter.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3556.76,
      "end": 3558.92,
      "text": "and also for all the mates of Mike Cross",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3558.92,
      "end": 3561.32,
      "text": "at [redacted address], Cottingham, North Underside",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3561.32,
      "end": 3563.92,
      "text": "that's Sean Sutton, Chris Knowles, Robert Kemp",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3563.92,
      "end": 3566.56,
      "text": "Ian Swale and Mike himself",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3566.56,
      "end": 3569.96,
      "text": "and all the other fellow heavy metal fans around the country",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3569.96,
      "end": 3575.14,
      "text": "right, it's time for the Friday Night Connection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3575.14,
      "end": 3577.94,
      "text": "at 1 minute and 20 seconds before 11 of the clock",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3577.94,
      "end": 3579.78,
      "text": "now the tracks that we played a couple of weeks ago",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3579.78,
      "end": 3582.9,
      "text": "as you remember there was no FNC last week because of the Zet concert",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3582.9,
      "end": 3585.08,
      "text": "the tracks we played a fortnight ago were",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3585.08,
      "end": 3588.74,
      "text": "It's a Plain Shame by Peter Frampton from the album Wind of Change",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3588.74,
      "end": 3595.06,
      "text": "all right now by free from the album fire and water and shame the devil by robin trower from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3595.06,
      "end": 3605.25,
      "text": "the album for earth below we didn't get one correct entry but we got a lot of entries that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3605.25,
      "end": 3610.15,
      "text": "gave us another answer which we think is equally as valid so we're going to give away the 10 pound",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3610.15,
      "end": 3617.75,
      "text": "record token now most people said it was the elements friday night connection 10 pound record",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3617.75,
      "end": 3630.01,
      "text": "token to simon tom of number 23 newton's way kitchen in hartfordshire it seems that the",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3630.01,
      "end": 3633.99,
      "text": "general consensus of opinion was that the fnc answer was shame so we'll accept that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3633.99,
      "end": 3638.67,
      "text": "and simon because of that executive decision you get yourself a 10 pound record token and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3638.67,
      "end": 3642.41,
      "text": "you also put together your own friday night connection have a listen folks",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3642.41,
      "end": 3649.61,
      "text": "friday night connection for tonight put together by simon tom of number",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3649.61,
      "end": 4632.47,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 3649.61,
      "end": 4632.47,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 4632.47,
      "end": 4635.05,
      "text": "[redacted address], Hitchin in Hertfordshire.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4635.43,
      "end": 4638.87,
      "text": "And just to recap on that, nobody got the right answer at all.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4639.11,
      "end": 4643.93,
      "text": "The general consensus of your opinion was that the answer to the FNC should have been shame.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4644.55,
      "end": 4648.21,
      "text": "So we thought it would have been a shame if we didn't actually award the ten quid to somebody.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4648.69,
      "end": 4650.59,
      "text": "So we did. We awarded it to Simon Tom.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4650.67,
      "end": 4651.89,
      "text": "That was his Friday night connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4652.33,
      "end": 4654.91,
      "text": "Three bits of music that have a definite connection.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4655.47,
      "end": 4660.45,
      "text": "Where it is, is for us and Simon to know at the moment and for you to let us know.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4660.45,
      "end": 4662.03,
      "text": "if indeed you know where it is at all.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4662.13,
      "end": 4663.45,
      "text": "It could be in the names of the artists,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4664.2,
      "end": 4665.24,
      "text": "names of the records,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4665.54,
      "end": 4667.08,
      "text": "it could be in the matrix numbers,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4667.3,
      "end": 4669.54,
      "text": "it could be the name of the dog of the producer,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4670.16,
      "end": 4671.9,
      "text": "absolutely anywhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4672.2,
      "end": 4673.66,
      "text": "But it's definitely in there somewhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4674.34,
      "end": 4675.62,
      "text": "If you think you know what it is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4676.2,
      "end": 4677.28,
      "text": "jot it down on the postcard,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4677.36,
      "end": 4678.74,
      "text": "any form of communication will do,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4678.82,
      "end": 4679.48,
      "text": "and send it to me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4679.58,
      "end": 4680.34,
      "text": "I'm Tommy Vance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4680.44,
      "end": 4680.86,
      "text": "Care of.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4681.32,
      "end": 4682.38,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4683.2,
      "end": 4684.4,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4685.06,
      "end": 4685.46,
      "text": "London,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4687.46,
      "end": 4688.42,
      "text": "W1A4WW.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4688.42,
      "end": 4690.82,
      "text": "you. Don't forget to put together your own",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4690.82,
      "end": 4691.96,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4692.74,
      "end": 4693.72,
      "text": "And bon chance.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4699.27,
      "end": 4700.73,
      "text": "1117, back to the archives.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4701.17,
      "end": 4702.97,
      "text": "1976, ACDC.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5357.29,
      "end": 5357.69,
      "text": "ACDC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5357.69,
      "end": 5359.99,
      "text": "from 1976. A couple of tracks",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5359.99,
      "end": 5362.09,
      "text": "there. High Voltage, which incidentally I'm sure",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5362.09,
      "end": 5363.87,
      "text": "you know was the title of their first album",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5363.87,
      "end": 5365.97,
      "text": "and also Little Lover. And that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5365.97,
      "end": 5367.91,
      "text": "unfortunately is all the ACDC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5367.91,
      "end": 5370.01,
      "text": "material we have because we only ever did one",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5370.01,
      "end": 5371.83,
      "text": "session with them. More's the pity",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5371.83,
      "end": 5373.85,
      "text": "because they're an ace band. I played that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5373.85,
      "end": 5375.93,
      "text": "for Laurie. That's a lady",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5375.93,
      "end": 5377.63,
      "text": "who lives down in Brighton from a gentleman",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5377.63,
      "end": 5379.35,
      "text": "from Withenshaw in Manchester.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5379.99,
      "end": 5381.97,
      "text": "A gentleman by the name of Cyril who met",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5381.97,
      "end": 5383.99,
      "text": "you when you both went to see ACDC",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5383.99,
      "end": 5385.91,
      "text": "at the Brighton Centre. He's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5385.91,
      "end": 5387.85,
      "text": "thinking about you, Laurie. Also for",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5387.85,
      "end": 5389.85,
      "text": "John McInnes of [redacted address]",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5389.85,
      "end": 5392.03,
      "text": "in Glasgow, and for everybody",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5392.03,
      "end": 5394.03,
      "text": "at the Seaford College from James Gurney,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5394.59,
      "end": 5395.97,
      "text": "that's Andy, both",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5395.97,
      "end": 5397.97,
      "text": "the Russes, Russell Castle, Russell Anderson,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5398.55,
      "end": 5400.15,
      "text": "Tim Frazzles, and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5400.15,
      "end": 5401.31,
      "text": "also Stu.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5401.91,
      "end": 5404.59,
      "text": "It's now 11.29, speak-o-dumb-one.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5405.45,
      "end": 5415.99,
      "text": "This Saturday at 4, Rock On stretches to three and a half hours,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5416.07,
      "end": 5419.93,
      "text": "and in the program you'll hear interviews with Simple Minds, The Inmates, and UFO.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5421.31,
      "end": 5437.59,
      "text": "We'll be celebrating the 10th anniversary of Radio 1's in concert,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5437.79,
      "end": 5441.01,
      "text": "and hearing the choice of the DJs who've introduced the show over the years.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5441.01,
      "end": 5444.71,
      "text": "This week's live set is by Roger Chapman and The Shortlist.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5455.22,
      "end": 5459.32,
      "text": "Brass in Pocket, number five in the BBC Top 30 from The Pretenders.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5459.86,
      "end": 5465.6,
      "text": "This Saturday, lead singer Chrissie Hynde reveals how she and her band intend to attack the ages.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5467.62,
      "end": 5470.2,
      "text": "The best of rock on and the best of in concert.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5470.68,
      "end": 5471.7,
      "text": "That's rock on Saturday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5472.0,
      "end": 5475.38,
      "text": "Join me, Tommy Vance, every week from 4 to 7.30.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5478.15,
      "end": 5480.03,
      "text": "Love the bit where he says, join me.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5480.09,
      "end": 5481.33,
      "text": "Why has he fallen apart?",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5481.33,
      "end": 5484.33,
      "text": "here is Chrissie Hynde",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5484.33,
      "end": 5486.41,
      "text": "and the pretenders and lovers of today",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5486.41,
      "end": 5489.41,
      "text": "that was Praying Mantis",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5580.0,
      "end": 6120.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5580.0,
      "end": 6120.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6120.79,
      "end": 6122.57,
      "text": "and Lovers to the Grave",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6122.57,
      "end": 6124.19,
      "text": "Praying Mantis, four piece band",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6124.19,
      "end": 6127.07,
      "text": "that's Tino Neofaitou and his brother Chris Neofaitou",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6127.07,
      "end": 6129.07,
      "text": "Peter Moore and Chris Hudson",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6129.07,
      "end": 6130.31,
      "text": "nice session",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6130.31,
      "end": 6132.27,
      "text": "Very nicely put together by Tony Wilson.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6132.77,
      "end": 6134.55,
      "text": "And prior to that, something from the Pretenders album.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6134.95,
      "end": 6137.21,
      "text": "The track was entitled Lovers of Today.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6137.85,
      "end": 6139.69,
      "text": "Now we're going to play some more by Sid Barrett.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6140.03,
      "end": 6142.55,
      "text": "Going to play three tracks that were recorded in 1970.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6143.21,
      "end": 6145.21,
      "text": "They're Gigolo Aunt, Two of a Kind,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6145.49,
      "end": 6148.11,
      "text": "and that delicate little thing that only lasts a minute",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6148.11,
      "end": 6149.99,
      "text": "called the Effervescing Elephant.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6150.57,
      "end": 6153.39,
      "text": "And this Sunday, it's Sid's birthday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6153.79,
      "end": 6155.71,
      "text": "Sid, wherever you are, happy birthday.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6155.71,
      "end": 6425.62,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6155.71,
      "end": 6425.62,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6430.62,
      "end": 6592.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6430.62,
      "end": 6592.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6592.7,
      "end": 6599.76,
      "text": "isn't that beautiful effervescing",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6599.76,
      "end": 6606.64,
      "text": "elephant sid barrett loads of people wanted to hear sid on the radio again just to name a few",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6606.64,
      "end": 6612.6,
      "text": "keith dunkey i think it is at number 58 skip lane in warsaw vince muir to the clock house high street",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6612.6,
      "end": 6617.84,
      "text": "henfield in sussex and also a lady or gentleman let me find out the name if i can",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6617.84,
      "end": 6620.92,
      "text": "that he's scrabbling around a gentleman, Simon Corkin,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6621.34,
      "end": 6625.1,
      "text": "at [redacted address], near Stoke-on-Trent.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6625.66,
      "end": 6628.16,
      "text": "When I was over there in Hollywood, said he, very flashily,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6628.24,
      "end": 6631.92,
      "text": "talking to Roger Waters to put together that Pink Floyd special of some weeks ago,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6632.3,
      "end": 6636.0,
      "text": "I asked Roger where Sid was, and he said, to the best of his knowledge,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6636.08,
      "end": 6638.74,
      "text": "he's on a farm in Cambridge, and he's happy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6639.9,
      "end": 6660.24,
      "text": "And, Sid, a very happy birthday for Sunday. Hello.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6660.48,
      "end": 6663.38,
      "text": "Hello, this is Steve Wright, the new boy on Radio 1.",
      "source": "Steve Wright"
    },
    {
      "start": 6663.38,
      "end": 6665.82,
      "text": "join me if you dare for my first show",
      "source": "Steve Wright"
    },
    {
      "start": 6665.82,
      "end": 6667.88,
      "text": "next Saturday night at 7.30",
      "source": "Steve Wright"
    },
    {
      "start": 6667.88,
      "end": 6669.44,
      "text": "that is this coming Saturday night",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6669.44,
      "end": 6670.54,
      "text": "tomorrow at 7.30",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6670.54,
      "end": 6672.2,
      "text": "join the new boy Steve Wright",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6672.2,
      "end": 6673.5,
      "text": "quick reminder about our address",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6673.5,
      "end": 6675.14,
      "text": "if you ever feel the urge to write to us",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6675.14,
      "end": 6678.02,
      "text": "for a request or maybe for an archive session",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6678.02,
      "end": 6678.98,
      "text": "do so",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6678.98,
      "end": 6681.12,
      "text": "we have openings now",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6681.12,
      "end": 6683.6,
      "text": "write to the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6683.6,
      "end": 6685.18,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6685.18,
      "end": 6687.94,
      "text": "London W1A4WW",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6687.94,
      "end": 6689.82,
      "text": "and we really do have openings",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6689.82,
      "end": 6691.68,
      "text": "for some good requests",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6691.68,
      "end": 6693.56,
      "text": "so why don't you start writing",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6693.56,
      "end": 6694.66,
      "text": "now",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6694.66,
      "end": 6698.26,
      "text": "Todd Rundgren and Just One Victory",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6698.26,
      "end": 7298.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 6698.26,
      "end": 7298.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7298.79,
      "end": 7300.73,
      "text": "for Caroline Pate from A Gentleman in Cheshire",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7300.73,
      "end": 7301.75,
      "text": "by the name of Steve Wallace",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7301.75,
      "end": 7303.65,
      "text": "and also for Claire Moose Bush",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7303.65,
      "end": 7304.55,
      "text": "Hermit Appanol",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7304.55,
      "end": 7305.89,
      "text": "The Wheat Hamster Mob You Heard",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7305.89,
      "end": 7308.45,
      "text": "Yank Me, Crank Me by Ted Nugent",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7308.45,
      "end": 7309.89,
